@startuml
!include ../style.puml
title Filesystem WAL, snapshots, and payload files
entity "manifest.jsonl" as Manifest <<file>> {
  one ManifestEntry per line
  v : 1
  block_number : i64
  root : optional snapshot root
  entries : u64
  ts_ms : i64
  sig : optional signature
}
entity "{root_hex}.wal" as Snapshot <<file>> {
  version : u8, currently 7
  count : u32 big-endian
  entries : custom binary WAL records
  identity : Blake2b-256(snapshot bytes)
}
entity "WAL record" as Wal {
  op / outcome : explicit tags
  path : logical root ID + relative path
  extra_path : optional logical path
  offset / length / payload_ref / mode / uid / gid
  other operation-specific fields
}
entity "{root_hex}.hashes" as Hashes <<file>> {
  referenced payload hashes
  retention sidecar paired with snapshot
}
entity "wal_payload_store/{payload_hash_hex}" as Payload <<file>> {
  raw payload bytes
  name : Blake2b-256(bytes)
}
entity "Provisioned filesystem" as Files <<files>> {
  logical root IDs map to operator paths
  files / directories / metadata
  consensus-static or dynamic provisioning
}
entity "Snapshot chunks" as Chunks <<transfer>> {
  4 MiB slices of snapshot bytes
  chunk hashes / Merkle proof steps
  not a separate LMDB table
}
Manifest --> Snapshot : optional root
Snapshot "1" --> "0..*" Wal
Snapshot --> Hashes : same root filename
Hashes --> Payload : retained payload hashes
Wal --> Payload : PayloadRef::Hash
Wal --> Files : logical path application
Chunks --> Snapshot : transfer representation
note bottom of Snapshot
SnapshotWriter selects the snapshot directory.
Atomic writes use temporary files and rename.
A snapshot can survive a failed manifest append.
Do not serialize validator-specific host paths as wire paths.
end note
legend bottom
Sources: rholang interpreter/io/snapshot.rs, wal.rs, snapshot_chunk.rs and casper engine/wal_payload_server.rs.
Full WAL variants and field declarations are in the memory inventory.
endlegend
@enduml
